{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117294","id":3379623839,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7JcPef","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117294","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117294.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117294.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117294","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117294/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117294/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117294/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/0b7c30fa350d2c8d9d60a535d31b572e848a6eb5","number":117294,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix `RenderingDevice::texture_clear()` behaving unexpectedly when using the D3D12 driver","user":{"login":"H3x4g0n","id":39725802,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NzI1ODAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39725802?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n","html_url":"https://github.com/H3x4g0n","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/H3x4g0n/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117210\r\n\r\nUsing `RenderingDevice::texture_clear()` led to different results between the Vulkan and D3D12 driver, depending on the `DataFormat` of the texture.\r\nThis PR changes the D3D12 driver to use `ID3D12GraphicsCommandList::ClearUnorderedAccessViewFloat()` for clearing color textures instead of `ID3D12GraphicsCommandList::ClearUnorderedAccessViewUint()`.\r\nAs far as my testing goes, this should make the result of `RenderingDevice::texture_clear()` be on par between the D3D12 and Vulkan driver.\r\n\r\nThe following example clears textures with different data formats to `Color.HOT_PINK` (left to right: `R8G8B8A8_UNORM`, `R32G32B32A32_SFLOAT`, `R8_UNORM`, `R32_SFLOAT`).\r\n\r\n**Before:**\r\n<img width=\"1940\" height=\"339\" alt=\"Before\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/425237d0-b727-41c3-9773-fa515b25facf\" />\r\n\r\n**This PR:**\r\n<img width=\"1940\" height=\"340\" alt=\"PR\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/65302aa9-ef02-4dc1-a241-0ae73d437489\" />\r\n\r\nExample project: [texture-clear-example.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25876690/texture-clear-example.zip)\r\n\r\nFrom what I've read about the behavior of those two clearing functions, I think that `ClearUnorderedAccessViewFloat()` would be more appropriate for clearing color textures.\r\nHowever, I am not sure whether I am missing something here that might cause issues, as I don't know whether there was a reason for using `ClearUnorderedAccessViewUint()` in the first place.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"mileston